<img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T07:47:34-08:00","id":34940,"title":"","content":"Oh, that would be awesome! An art book with art from all the game lines over the entire run of classic World of Darkness would be glorious!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T09:25:25-08:00","id":34967,"title":"","content":"I don't think that it was lost due to &quot;downsizing&quot;, but rather 20 years of improper back-ups, corrupted files, different software that no longer exists/is supported on hardware you have to purchase on Ebay to acquire, etc.. (<i>What do you mean I can't access my files on my 1994 Apple SCSI SyQuest 100MB external file storage cartridge?</i>)<br /> For W20, Rich went into the archives, apparently an un-organized storage of old artwork that had been kept in-house and spent quite some time trying to hunt down all of the pieces and then re-scanned Josh Timbrook's &quot;Flip Book of Death&quot;. But not all of the artwork was kept, and much may have gone back to the artists and sold to private collectors over the decades too, leaving only the original scans, or what is found in the books (likely not necessarily great for archived material).<br /> <br /> There were art books released, like &quot;The Artwork of Werewolf: the Apocalypse&quot; that you can find on <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/THE-ART-OF-WEREWOLF-APOCALYPSE/dp/1588463028\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon</a> and <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3373/The-Art-of-Werewolf-the-Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThruRPG</a> , as well as for <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/287/The-Art-of-Mage-the-Ascension/\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: the Ascension</a> and <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/2278/Art-of-Vampire-The-Masquerade-%28WW2298%29\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: the Masquerade</a>.<br /> <br /> Right now it's tough enough to get Rich to complete, or update us on the W20 KickStarter &quot;The Making of the Artwork for Werewolf: the Apocalypse 20th Anniversary Edition&quot;, so even if they had all of the original art pieces, I highly doubt we'll see anything so cool as coffee table book of many of the awesome pieces created over the years for the CWoD. :-(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/